      <h1 class="visually-hidden">litmus</h1>
    </div>
    <p>Litmus runs a malware classifier against files, archives, and
    processes. Hand it a path; it scans, classifies, and exits with a
    status code you can act on in CI. Whatever
    <a href="/cleave/">cleave</a> decomposes, litmus classifies — across
    20+ languages and six binary formats.</p>
    <p>The reference model is <a href="/azoth/">azoth</a> (releasing
    soon). Litmus runs any model trained on cleave's capability schema.
    Decision thresholds are tunable per call
    (<code>--threshold-hostile</code>, <code>--threshold-suspicious</code>).
    If the defaults don't match your threat model, override them; if the
    model doesn't either, bring your own.</p>

    <h2>Capabilities</h2>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>File scanning</strong> — files, directories, and archives, classified against a local <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/litmus-models/" target="_blank">ML model</a></li>
      <li><strong>Process scanning</strong> — running processes, by way of the on-disk image (memory-resident analysis is not yet implemented)</li>
      <li><strong>Pluggable models</strong> — designed around azoth, but runs any model trained on cleave's capability schema</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Differential analysis — comparing two versions of a package to
    surface newly-introduced malicious capabilities — is in development.
    It's aimed at catching compromised dependency updates, where the
    signal is the diff, not the artifact.</p>

    <h2>Install</h2>

Homebrew (macOS or Linux):

<pre class="install-block">
brew tap atomdrift/tap https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/homebrew-tap.git

brew install atomdrift/tap/litmus
</pre>

From source

<pre class="install-block">
git clone --depth 1 https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/litmus.git
make install
</pre>

    <h2>Usage</h2>
    <pre class="install-block">$ litmus scan &lt;path&gt;</pre>

    <p style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 0.8125rem;">For more thorough results, install
    <a href="https://github.com/rizinorg/rizin" target="_blank">Rizin</a> (binary reverse-engineering) and
    <a href="https://github.com/upx/upx" target="_blank">UPX</a> (unpacker).</p>

